// cppcheck suppressions: one per intentional violation.
// Format: <id>:<file>:<line>  followed by `// audit:<ID> <rationale>`.
// File-wide form `<id>:<file>` and project-wide `<id>:*` also accepted.
//
// Common categories to expect:
//   missingIncludeSystem  — system includes intentionally not parsed
//   unusedFunction        — public C API consumed by tests/ + external embedders
//                           (cppcheck scans src/ only — every public-API entry
//                           point looks unused from its perspective)
//   constParameterCallback— argv const-cast would cascade into every callback
//                           function-pointer site; cppcheck flags this itself

// =============================================================================
// Project-wide: unusedFunction (Phase 19)
// =============================================================================
// audit:CPPCHK-009 (Phase 19) — cppcheck scans src/ only; the public C API
// surface (urbi_*, helper definitions used by tests/, native callbacks invoked
// via function-pointer tables) is structurally unreachable from cppcheck's
// call-graph view.  Suppressing the whole category project-wide is correct
// here: removing or marking-static any public-API symbol would break
// test/ binaries or external embedders.  Re-evaluate if cppcheck gains
// cross-TU resolution for header-declared exports.
unusedFunction

// =============================================================================
// src/vm/uvm.c — computed-goto dispatch table
// =============================================================================
// audit:CPPCHK-010 (Phase 19) — cppcheck cannot parse GCC's label-address
// operator `&&label` (it sees `&&` as logical-and producing a bool), so it
// flags every dispatch_table entry as `assignBoolToPointer` and every
// `label_OP_*:` target as `unusedLabelConfiguration` (claiming the labels
// only exist under preprocessor branches).  Both are correctness-stable
// false positives: UVM_USE_COMPUTED_GOTO=1 is the host build mode, the
// labels are jumped to via `goto *dispatch_table[opcode]` at the dispatch
// hot loop (src/vm/uvm.c near line 290).  Suppressing file-wide because
// every opcode handler is affected.
assignBoolToPointer:src/vm/uvm.c
unusedLabelConfiguration:src/vm/uvm.c

// =============================================================================
// Per-site suppressions
// =============================================================================

// audit:CPPCHK-002 lookup_id rollover guard — three sites where cppcheck's
// static analysis assumes 32-bit lookup_id and reports the (uint32_t) cast on
// (lookup_id + 1ULL) as always false.  vm->lookup_id is uint64_t; the cast
// catches the actual u32 wrap (every ~4B lookups) where the stamp would
// collide with the "no stamp" sentinel 0.  Guard is live correctness on
// 64-bit hosts and required for stamp-uniqueness during DFS traversal.
// Verified 2026-05-08 against src/vm/uvm.h:128 (uint64_t lookup_id field).
knownConditionTrueFalse:src/object/uobject_lookup.c:86
knownConditionTrueFalse:src/object/uobject_lookup.c:124
knownConditionTrueFalse:src/object/uobject_slot.c:543

// audit:CPPCHK-011 (Phase 19) — pattern_matches() is an M3 catch-everything
// stub that always returns 1 (src/runtime/uunwind.c:65 docstring); cppcheck
// correctly flags the call-site as `always true`.  M5 refines pattern dispatch
// to actual exception-class matching (see comment block at uunwind.c:55-62);
// suppressing keeps the gate green until that lands.
knownConditionTrueFalse:src/runtime/uunwind.c:275

// audit:CPPCHK-012 (Phase 19) — urbi_native_event_waituntil's signature is
// dictated by the native-event callback function-pointer type registered
// via event_native_register; declaring `argv` const here would cascade
// into casts at every callback registration site.  cppcheck itself notes
// the callback caveat in the diagnostic.  Equivalent native callbacks
// in src/event/uevent_native.c don't trigger this because they're called
// directly (not via function-pointer table); only this one is.
constParameterCallback:src/event/uevent_native.c:170

// audit:CPPCHK-013 (Phase 19) — parse_err_line / parse_err_col are written
// in the parse-error breakout (lines 141-142) and read inside the
// `__STDC_HOSTED__` guarded snprintf at line 164-167.  Under freestanding
// builds the read-side is preprocessed out, leaving the write apparently
// dead — cppcheck doesn't track the configuration-conditional read.
// The values are correctness-needed under hosted builds (REPL diagnostics)
// and dead under freestanding builds (where the only outcome is a fixed
// "compile error" string fallback).
unreadVariable:src/module/uchunk.c:136
unreadVariable:src/module/uchunk.c:141
unreadVariable:src/module/uchunk.c:142
